      "id": "bbc-2026-05-26-starmer-vows-to-act-on-social-media-after-meeting-bereaved-p",
      "title": "Starmer vows to act on social media after meeting bereaved parents",
      "summary": "Some parents believe whether the government will take strong enough action remains to be seen.",
      "body": "1 day agoLiv McMahon,technology reporter,Zoe Kleinman,technology editorandHugh Pym,health editorReutersThe Prime Minister Sir Keir Starmer has vowed to take \"decisive\" action to tackle the impact of social media on UK children, as the government's consultation on the matter draws to a close.Sir Keir told families and campaigners who insist their children died as a result of social media use that \"it is important that we act and will act\".Speaking ahead of a meeting with them on Tuesday, the Prime Minister had said he was clear action must be a \"game-changer\" amid calls to ban social media for under-16s.But some parents believe whether the government will take strong enough action remains to be seen.\"Am I confident? Definitely not,\" said Ellen Roome, speaking to the BBC outside 10 Downing Street after a meeting with the prime minister.\"I think we've heard it so many times before,\" she said - adding that until she sees change actually happen she will remain \"sceptical\".He told the BBC he would \"like to believe\" Sir Keir will take action but said at the moment the \"same status quo\" remains - with tech firms rolling out products including AI chatbots at pace.Members of the group told reporters the meeting had been a \"listening exercise\" for the Prime Minister and they had \"put it all out on the table\" in a bid to effect change.\"We do not want this group to grow any further,\" one parent said. \"We want all our asks to be adhered to.\"Another added they \"wanted no more children to die as a result of online harm\".PA MediaMariano Janin (left) and Ellen Roome were among the parents who spoke to the prime ministerIt comes after former health secretary Wes Streeting joined those calling for a ban of under-16s from social media in the UK.He said that big tech had used tactics similar to big tobacco in designing addictive platforms that posed harms to children. \"The precautionary principle should apply here,\" he said - adding that the government should act quickly and the UK is \"behind the curve\" on the issue.Streeting said he was now \"liberated\" to speak more freely about the issue since he quit his government post, but trusted Technology Secretary Liz Kendall \"to act quickly following the closure of the consultation today\".Kendall has said new measures for under-16s will be brought in by the end of 2026.Consulting on measuresBanning social apps for under-16s, as has happened in Australia, is one of the options being considered.Kendall said a response to the consultation would be published in the summer.Campaigners are broadly split on whether an outright ban on social apps for children is the best approach.Since March, the government has been asking parents and children if measures including app curfews and stronger age checks would improve online safety, and trialled these in some UK homes.\"The question isn't whether we're going to act - we will,\" Kendall told the BBC.She said the government's scope was looking at a broad range of issues and features and how these affected children.This could see the UK look more closely at platforms not covered by Australia's restrictions, such as Roblox and Discord.But Kendall said the government wanted to hear \"all views\" from the consultation, which closes at the end of Tuesday.\"We've got to get this right, and we've got to make it last,\" she added.The government is learning lessons from Australia's social media ban, Liz Kendall told BBC BreakfastThe consultation has seen more than 80,000 submissions from charities, campaign groups and members of the public who have given their views on a ban or other interventions.Government data obtained by the Press Association on Tuesday showed 42,410 parents and 13,890 young people have filled in the survey.People were also asked for opinions on possible restrictions, including night-time curfews or features such as auto-play and infinite scroll being disabled.A number of organisations, ranging from police leaders to children's groups and trade bodies, have already shared views on what should be done.Donya Soni-Clark, associate director of trade association TechUK, also told Today that \"regulating by features, not by platform\" would be the best way forward.Meanwhile in a submission published on Tuesday, the Academy of Medical Royal Colleges, said doctors should routinely ask younger patients about their device and social media use.Its response, which presented screen time and social media use as a parallel problem, also cited examples of physical and mental health issues caused by watching extreme violence online.There is no consensus among the wider scientific community that screen time overall is harmful to children.But Academy Chair Jeanette Dickson said that like smoking or seatbelts before, the issue had become a \"unifying force\" for the profession.It is not the first time screen time and social media have been likened to smoking in posing risks to people's health and wellbeing.Streeting told Today that tech whistleblower testimonies over the years had highlighted similar industry practice and awareness of known harms.\"They know that the product they're designing is addictive, they know that it is harmful, and the business model is orientated towards getting kids while they're young,\" he said.Lord Nash, a former Conservative education minister, said the government had committed to parliament that it would introduce some age or functionality limits on social media for children.He said it must \"deliver on that commitment fully and in the shortest possible timeframe.\"Children in Australia tell UK kids how a social media ban has affected themBut some campaigners believe stopping social media access would fail children.Ian Russell, chair of the online safety charity the Molly Rose Foundation, has previously said the government should enforce existing laws rather than bring in \"sledgehammer techniques like bans\".An open letter signed by child safety charities said the government should make tech firms align with the British Board of Film Classification (BBFC), which determines film age ratings, to protect teens \"in line with the same high standards applied to film released in UK cinemas\".\"Hundreds of millions of websites are already classified to our standards and filtered by the mobile network operators,\" the BBFC's Chief Executive, David Austin, told the BBC.\"Why can't social media companies do the same in terms of their content? The answer is they can,\" he said.It is unclear which tech platforms have responded to the government's consultation or proposals to ban social media for under-16s in the UK.But Meta, which owns Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp, has said it wants age verification to be handled on a device level, so underage children would be blocked from downloading certain apps.Kendall told the BBC she would take action even if big tech pushes back.\"No one's going to stop me from doing what I think is right for this country,\" she said.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-05-26T16:29:53.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/branded_news/b751/live/1942fc20-591d-11f1-8b8c-6d33e1d5abb6.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5y7r9gqp6jo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 6,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "theverge-2026-05-26-the-best-memorial-day-sales-you-can-still-shop",
      "title": "The best Memorial Day sales you can still shop",
      "summary": "You can still save $200 on the new MacBook Air. | Photo: Antonio G. Di Benedetto / The Verge\t\n\nThe long weekend is over, but many of the best Memorial Day deals are still available. Many of our favorite portable speakers are discounted, as are other outdoorsy products we like, including a set of solar lights. You can also find deals on everything from 4K OLED TVs and noise-canceling earbuds to lap",
      "body": "The long weekend is over, but many of the best Memorial Day deals are still available. Many of our favorite portable speakers are discounted, as are other outdoorsy products we like, including a set of solar lights. You can also find deals on everything from 4K OLED TVs and noise-canceling earbuds to laptops, and plenty of our favorite everyday essentials.\nTo give you more options, we’ve also included a selection of deals from retailers that weren’t officially running Memorial Day sales but are still matching many of the same prices.\nSavings are savings, after all.\nApple 13-inch MacBook Air (M5)\nNintendo Switch 2 “Choose Your Game” bundle\n[Product: Nothing Headphone A | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G6LCC42J/?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.nothing.tech%2Fproducts%2Fheadphone-a%3FColour%3DBlack]\n[Product: Bose QuietComfort Ultra Earbuds (2nd Gen) | https://www.amazon.com/Bose-New-QuietComfort-Ultra-Earbuds/dp/B0F7M3HPBD?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FBose-QuietComfort-Ultra-Earbuds-II-Wireless-Noise-Cancelling-Earbuds-White%2F15864510101, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fbose-quietcomfort-ultra-2nd-gen-true-wireless-noise-cancelling-in-ear-earbuds-black%2FJ7C5V6WCKZ]\n* Samsung’s Galaxy Buds 3 Pro are on sale for $149.99 ($100 off) at Best Buy, which matches their all-time low price. The wireless earbuds are our top pick for Samsung Galaxy phone device owners, thanks to their comfortable AirPods-inspired design, terrific sound quality, and good noise cancellation. They also offer helpful voice controls that let you adjust volume or playback without a wake word, while delivering excellent voice call quality. Read our review.\n* If you’re an Apple user, there’s no better pair of starter buds than the open-style&nbsp;AirPods 4, which have fallen to $99 ($30 off) at&nbsp;Walmart. The latest model sounds significantly better than the third-gen pair, particularly for voice calls. More importantly, they offer robust integration with the rest of the Apple ecosystem, letting you take advantage of audio sharing, automatic device switching, hands-free “Hey Siri” commands, Apple TV integration, and more.&nbsp;Read our review.\n[Product: Nothing Ear (a) | https://www.amazon.com/Nothing-Ear-Integration-Cancelling-Equaliser/dp/B0CXPRP216/?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.nothing.tech%2Fproducts%2Fear-a%3FColour%3DBlack]\n* Sennheiser’s Momentum True Wireless 4 earbuds are down to around $199.95 ($100 off) at Amazon and Best Buy, which is $20 shy of their best price to date. If sound quality matters most, they’re an easy recommendation, delivering rich, detailed audio with EQ customization to fine-tune the listening experience. Optional wing tips are included to help keep them secure and comfortable. Read our review.\n* Walmart‘s selling the last-gen AirPods Max (USB-C) for around $449 ($100 off), which is $50 shy of their all-time low. Apple’s luxe over-ear headphones offer a premium design and work especially well with other Apple devices. They still deliver great sound quality and effective noise cancellation, even if the newer model has a slight edge. Read our review.\n[Product: CMF Buds Pro 2 | https://www.amazon.com/CMF-Buds-Pro-Cancelling-Technology/dp/B0D83J6JJ9/?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fus.nothing.tech%2Fproducts%2Fcmf-buds-pro-2%3FColour%3DOrange]\n[Product: Sony WH-1000XM5 | https://www.amazon.com/Sony-WH-1000XM5-Canceling-Headphones-Hands-Free/dp/B09XS7JWHH/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fsony-wh-1000xm5-wireless-noise-canceling-over-the-ear-headphones-black%2FJ7XSRH5CXG%2Fsku%2F6505727%2F, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Fsony-wh-1000xm5-bluetooth-wireless-noise-canceling-headphones-black%2F-%2FA-86314264]\n[Product: Sonos Move 2 | https://www.amazon.com/Sonos-Move-Wireless-Portable-Bluetooth/dp/B0CGGYYK2D/?tag=theverge02-20, https://sonos.sjv.io/c/482924/2804767/32256?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sonos.com%2Fen-us%2Fshop%2Fmove-2, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fsonos-move-2-portable-durable-smart-speaker-each-black%2FJ39H373KJK]\n* JBL’s Flip 7 speaker is on sale for $99.95 ($50 off) at Amazon and Best Buy,&nbsp; which matches its best price to date. The portable Bluetooth speaker builds on the Flip 6 with more durable IP68 dust and water resistance and improved sound that can reach higher volumes without sounding harsh. JBL’s new PushLock system also lets you easily swap in accessories, like the included wrist strap.\n* Bose’s SoundLink Plus is down to $209 ($50 off) at Amazon, Best Buy, and directly from Bose, which is its second-best price this year and $30 shy of its all-time low. In his review, The Verge’s John Higgins called it a “great beach speaker,” as it offers impressively loud sound for its size, up to 20 hours of battery life, and a durable IP67-rated design that can handle pool days. Read our review.\n[Product: JBL Charge 6 | https://www.amazon.com/JBL-Charge-Waterproof-Drop-Proof-Built/dp/B0DN35M7S9/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fjbl-charge-6-portable-wireless-speaker-2025-blue%2FJ7LXFW3JFQ, https://rei.pxf.io/c/482924/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F255217%2Fjbl-charge-6-bt-speaker]\n* Bose’s SoundLink Micro is on sale for $99 ($30 off) at Amazon and Best Buy , matching its all-time low price. It’s a good pick if you want something more portable than the larger SoundLink Plus. It won’t deliver the same room-filling sound, but it’s pocket-friendly, features a rugged IP67 design, and offers up to 12 hours of battery life, making it easier to take on the go.\n* The portable Beats Pill speaker is on sale for $99.99 ($50 off) at Amazon, Best Buy, and Walmart. The pill-shaped speaker improves on its predecessor with up to 24 hours of battery life on a single charge, while adding two-way USB-C charging and lossless audio support. It also introduces an IP67-rated design and native Find My support on both Android and iOS if it goes missing. Read our review.\n[Product: Sonos Roam 2 | https://www.amazon.com/Sonos-Roam-Portable-Waterproof-Bluetooth/dp/B0CY6S748H/?tag=theverge02-20, https://sonos.sjv.io/c/482924/2804767/32256?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.sonos.com%2Fen-us%2Fshop%2Froam-2-black%2F, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fsonos-roam-2-portable-smart-speaker-with-waterproof-and-dustproof-design-each-black%2FJ39H3735KG]\n[Product: LG B5 OLED TV | https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Flg-77-class-b5-series-oled-ai-4k-uhd-smart-webos-tv-2025%2FJJ8VPZTKZW%2Fsku%2F6621813]\n[Product: LG C5 OLED TV | https://www.amazon.com/LG-Upscaling-Filmmaker-Orchestra-OLED77C5PUA/dp/B0DYQM4BDB/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Flg-65-class-c5-series-oled-evo-ai-4k-uhd-smart-webos-tv-2025%2FJJ8VPZTRG6]\n* Multiple configurations of Sony’s Bravia 8 II TV are on sale, with the 65-inch on sale for around $2,598 at Amazon, Best Buy, and directly from Sony — its second-best price so far this year. Crowned the “king of TV” in Value Electronics’&nbsp;2025 shootout, the exceptionally bright OLED TV boasts excellent color accuracy and a snappy 120Hz refresh rate. It also runs on Google TV and supports both Apple AirPlay 2 and Google Cast. Read our review.\n* The latest&nbsp;Amazon Fire TV Cube&nbsp;is on sale at&nbsp;Amazon and Best Buy for $109.99 ($30 off), which is its second-best price of the year but $30 more than its all-time low. Amazon’s latest Fire TV Cube combines a 4K streaming box with an Echo speaker, letting you play music, stream content in Dolby Vision, HDR, and Dolby Atmos, and control your TV and other smart home devices with hands-free Alexa voice commands. It also supports Wi-Fi 6E for faster, more reliable connectivity.\n[Product: Amazon Fire TV Stick 4K Plus | https://www.amazon.com/Amazon-newest-AI-powered-Search-million/dp/B0F7Z4QZTT/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Famazon-fire-tv-stick-4k-plus-newest-model-ai-powered-fire-tv-search-wi-fi-6-streaming-device-8-gb-free-live-tv-black%2FJ39TLS6QVZ%2Fsku%2F6644638, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Famazon-fire-tv-stick-4k-2024%2F-%2FA-91651394]\n* If you want a little more speed and storage than Amazon’s Fire TV Stick 4K Plus offers, its 4K Max is&nbsp;on sale for $39.99 ($20 off) at Amazon, Best Buy, and Target, which is $5 shy of its all-time low. It, too, runs on the new and improved Fire TV OS and supports Dolby Vision, HDR10 Plus, and Dolby Atmos. However, it adds faster performance, double the storage (16GB), and Wi-Fi 6E support. It also comes with a more capable remote, the Alexa Voice Remote Enhanced, which adds a button for live TV channel listings. Read our review.\n[Product: Hisense CanvasTV | https://www.amazon.com/Hisense-65-Inch-CanvasTVTM-Vision-65S7N/dp/B0D2PNVJFT/?th=1&tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fhisense-65-class-s7-series-canvastv-4k-qled-tv-with-hi-matte-display-and-ultraslim-wall-mount-2024%2FJ3Z9Z4234Y]\n[Product: Samsung S95F | https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fsamsung-65-class-s95f-series-oled-4k-uhd-samsungvision-ai-smart-tizen-tv-2025%2FJ3ZYG2VV3P, https://www.amazon.com/SAMSUNG-65-Inch-Processor-Xcelerator-Samsung/dp/B0DXMJFJ7W?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: SwitchBot Bot Rechargeable | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GQPWD5BT/?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.switch-bot.com%2Fproducts%2Fswitchbot-bot-rechargeable]\n[Product: Dyson PencilWash | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GKJ1PYJZ/?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.target.com/c/482924/81938/2092?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.target.com%2Fp%2Fdyson-pencilwash-cordless-wet-hard-floor-cleaner-brown%2F-%2FA-95266540%23lnk%3Dsametab, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.dyson.com%2Ffloor-cleaners%2Fwet%2Fpencilwash%2Fcopper]\n[Product: Ring Battery Doorbell Plus (second-gen) | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F14N7HHH/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fring-battery-doorbell-plus-newest-model-retinal-2k-with-wide-angle-video-up-to-6x-zoom-night-vision-and-battery-pack-nickel-silver%2FJ39TLSRS6P%2Fsku%2F6672122, https://ring.pxf.io/c/482924/3022805/30431?u=https%3A%2F%2Fring.com%2Fproducts%2Fbattery-doorbell-plus-2nd-gen%2Fcolor%2Fpolishednightnavy]\n* Ecobee’s Smart Thermostat Premium is on sale for $229.99 ($30 off) at Amazon and directly from Ecobee, which is within $30 of its lowest price to date. The high-end&nbsp;smart thermostat can adjust temperatures based on where you are in your home, send alerts if your home gets too hot or cold while you’re away, and even track basic indoor air quality metrics like humidity, VOCs, and carbon dioxide. It also works well with Alexa, Siri, Apple Home, Google Home, SmartThings, and IFTTT, while doubling as a decent smart speaker. Read our review.\n* If you don’t need all the features offered by Ecobee’s top-tier model, Ecobee’s Smart Thermostat Enhanced is on sale for $169.99 ($30 off) at Amazon and directly from Ecobee, which is one of its better prices so far this year. It also adjusts temperatures based on whether anyone’s home and works with Alexa, Apple Home, Google Home, and SmartThings. Compared to the Premium model, though, you can’t use it as a doorbell, and it lacks indoor air quality monitoring and built-in voice control.\n[Product: Birdfy Feeder | https://www.amazon.com/NETVUE-Birdfy-Watching-Capture-Detection/dp/B0B56BVWBM/?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.birdfy.com%2Fproducts%2Flimited-gift-edition-for-birdfy-feeder, https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0B56BFH7P/?tag=theverge02-20]\n[Product: Ecovacs Deebot X9 Pro Omni | https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fecovacs-robotics-deebot-x9-pro-omni-robot-vacuum-mop-real-time-self-washing-mopping-blast-16600pa-suction-triple-auto-mop-lift-black%2FJ3R8442FWT, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://www.ecovacs.com/us/deebot-robotic-vacuum-cleaner/deebot-x9-pro-omni/]\n[Product: Coway Airmega AP-1512HH Mighty air purifier | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B01728NLRG/?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FCoway-Air-Purifier-Airmega-AP-1512HH-White-True-HEPA-3-Stages-Filtration-System-with-361-Sq-Ft-Coverage-Auto-Eco-Mode%2F194187883]\n* Ecobee’s Smart Thermostat Essential is on sale for $119.99 ($20 off) at Amazon and directly from Ecobee, which is also one of its better prices in recent months. The company’s most affordable thermostat covers the basics, letting you control your home’s temperature, create schedules in the app, and use Alexa, Apple Home, or Google Assistant. It also sends intruder alerts, but unlike Ecobee’s pricier models, it can’t automatically adjust temperatures based on activity in your home.\n[Product: Ring Floodlight Cam Wired Pro | https://www.amazon.com/Ring-Floodlight-Cam-Wired-Pro/dp/B08FCWQWDZ/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fsite%2Fring-floodlight-cam-pro-with-2k-video-and-ring-vision-2-led-lights-dual-band-wi-fi-and-3d-motion-detection-white%2F6456121.p, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.homedepot.com%2Fp%2FRing-Floodlight-Cam-Pro-Smart-Wired-Outdoor-Security-Camera-with-2-LED-Lights-3D-Motion-Detection-Dual-Band-WiFi-White-B0CG6VFFVL%2F329107033]\n[Product: Ecobee Smart Doorbell Camera | https://www.amazon.com/ecobee-Smart-Video-Doorbell-Camera/dp/B0C424CVZ8/?tag=theverge02-20, https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=nOD/rLJHOac&mid=46044&murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ecobee.com%2Fen-us%2Fsmart-doorbell-camera-wired%2F]\n[Product: Eve Energy Smart Plug | https://www.amazon.com/Eve-Energy-Matter-Control-SmartThings/dp/B0BZBGD87V?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Feve-energy-smart-plug-matter-white%2FJ3L3KQ4LQ6%2Fsku%2F6546393, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.homedepot.com%2Fp%2Feve-Energy-Matter-Smart-Plug-Matter-Thread-Enabled-works-w-Apple-Home-SmartThings-Alexa-Google-Home-White-10037863%2F326969071]\n[Product: Nintendo Switch 2 “Choose Your Game” bundle | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GZ5DFHC5/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fswitch-2-choose-your-game-bundle-nintendo-switch-2%2FJ7GSL57WQR, https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=nOD/rLJHOac&mid=24348&murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.gamestop.com%2Fconsoles-hardware%2Fnintendo-switch-2%2Fproducts%2Fnintendo-switch-2-choose-your-game-bundle%2F445803.html]\n[Product: Metroid Prime 4: Beyond | https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fmetroid-prime-4-beyond-nintendo-switch-oled-model-nintendo-switch-nintendo-switch-lite%2FJ7GSL484KF]\n* You can save $100 when you spend over $400 on select Logitech products at Best Buy. The limited-time promo includes Logitech’s $179.99 Pro X2 Superstrike gaming mouse, which uses haptics-based buttons instead of mechanical ones, along with Logitech’s G923 racing wheel and its A50 Lightspeed gaming headset. The promo details are located under the pricing on each landing page, nested within the “Special Offers” section. From there, you can build your bundle.\n[Product: Star Wars Outlaws | https://www.amazon.com/Star-Wars-Outlaws-Gold-Nintendo-Switch/dp/B0F79Z9V31/?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FStar-Wars-Outlaws-PlayStation-5%2F5439978114%3F]\n[Product: Xbox Wireless Controller | https://www.amazon.com/Xbox-Wireless-Gaming-Controller-Headsets-Console/dp/B0F1HTGDTL?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FMicrosoft-Xbox-Wireless-Controller-Carbon-Black%2F15074463540, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fmicrosoft-xbox-wireless-controller-for-xbox-series-x-xbox-series-s-xbox-one-pcs-and-cloud-enabled-devices-robot-white%2FJJGXPXQ2VS]\n[Product: iPad (2025) | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DZ75TN5F/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DZ76LW4J/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DZ75HDQ4/?tag=theverge02-20]\n* The latest 11-inch iPad Pro with 256GB of storage is down to $899 ($100 off) at Amazon, which is $100 shy of its all-time low. If you prefer a bigger screen, the 13-inch / Wi-Fi model with 256GB of storage is also on sale at Amazon for around $1,195 ($105 off). Apple’s newest iPad Pro is its fastest tablet yet, packing the M5 chip along with faster storage speeds, quicker charging, and a new N1 chip that handles wireless connectivity like Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and Thread. Read our review.\n* TCL’s Note A1 Nxtpaper is a tablet primarily for note-taking, akin to Remarkable’s Paper Pure and Amazon’s Kindle Scribe, but with a much better screen. You can currently snag the 11.5-inch tablet with a keyboard cover for $499.99 (originally $599.99) directly from TCL’s online storefront. The tablet features a 120Hz color panel that feels natural to draw or write on with its included stylus; it also offers a slew of built-in AI tools, allowing you to convert handwriting to text, make your handwriting more legible, and carry out other actions.\n[Product: Apple 13-inch MacBook Air (M5) | https://www.amazon.com/Apple-2026-MacBook-13-inch-Laptop/dp/B0GR1493ZV/?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2F13-inch-macbook-air-apple-m5-chip-with-10-core-cpu-and-8-core-gpu-16gb-memory-512gb-ssd-midnight%2FJJGCQLKXL7]\n[Product: Anker Laptop Power Bank | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DCBB2YTR/?tag=theverge02-20, https://goto.walmart.com/c/482924/565706/9383?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.walmart.com%2Fip%2FAnker-Power-Bank-25K-165W-Built-In-and-Retractable-Cables%2F15136063005, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fanker-laptop-power-bank-25k-165w-built-in-and-retractable-cables-black%2FJJ858RXPXJ]\n[Product: Anker Nano Charger (45W, Smart Display, 180° Foldable) | https://www.amazon.com/Anker-Charging-Foldable-Recognition-Non-Battery/dp/B0G1MRLXMV?tag=theverge02-20, https://anker.pxf.io/c/482924/1543964/18023?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.anker.com%2Fproducts%2Fa121d-45w-usb-c-fast-charger-foldable-plug-compact]\n* Satechi’s 3-in-1 Foldable Wireless Charging Stand with Qi2 25W is on sale for $116.99 ($13 off) at Amazon, which is a new low price. The adjustable, foldable stand can wirelessly deliver up to 25W to compatible iPhones while simultaneously fast charging an Apple Watch and topping up your AirPods, but it also works with a range of Qi, Qi2, and Qi2.2-compatible Android phones and wireless earbuds. Satechi&nbsp;also includes a 45W USB-C adapter along with three international adapters, making it a useful travel companion.\n[Product: Jackery Explorer 500 | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07SM5HBK1?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.jackery.com%2Fproducts%2Fexplorer-500w-portable-power-station]\n* Goal Zero is taking 25 percent off a range of portable power stations, including the Yeti 700, which is currently $524.89 ($175 off). The portable power station can power up to nine devices at once through its AC, USB-C, USB-A, and 12V ports. Compared to the smaller Yeti 300 (on sale for $262.89) and Yeti 500 (on sale for $374.89), the higher-end model offers greater battery capacity and power output, making it a better fit for running multiple laptops, phones, lights, and even small appliances simultaneously.\n[Product: Shargeek 170 Power Bank | https://www.amazon.com/SHARGEEK-Portable-Charger-Display-Waterproof/dp/B0D2VWVPRX/ref=sr_1_1?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fsharge.com%2Fproducts%2Fshargeek-170%2F]\n[Product: Garmin inReach Mini 2 | https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B09PSKG7C3/?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://www.garmin.com/en-US/p/765374]\n* The Insta360 Link 2 Pro is down to $229.99 ($20 off) at Amazon, Best Buy, and directly from Insta360. The premium 4K webcam uses a large 1/1.3-inch sensor for sharper image quality and better low-light performance than its predecessor, though its resolution still maxes out at 4K/30fps or 1080p at up to 60fps. It features a two-axis gimbal and dual microphones with AI noise cancellation, while retaining features like AI tracking to help keep you centered if you move around.\n[Product: Ray-Ban Meta (Gen 1) smart glasses | https://www.amazon.com/Ray-Ban-Smart-Glasses-Wayfarer-Shiny-Black/dp/B0CGXYM9TP?tag=theverge02-20, https://bestbuy.7tiv.net/c/482924/614286/10014?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bestbuy.com%2Fproduct%2Fray-ban-meta-wayfarer-glasses-with-meta-ai-audio-photo-video-compatibility-green-lenses-shiny-black%2FBCKVZQ48PC, https://www.meta.com/ai-glasses/wayfarer-shiny-black-clear/]\n* You can buy the&nbsp;Insta360 X5&nbsp;at Amazon,&nbsp;Best Buy, and directly from&nbsp;Insta360’s online storefront&nbsp;for an all-time low of $464.99 ($85 off), with Insta360 throwing in a free lens kit. The 360-degree action cam delivers sharper, more detailed images than its predecessor and improved low-light performance. Specifically, it now allows you to capture 4K footage at up to 120fps, 8K video at up to 30fps, or 5.7K at 60fps, while offering support for user-replaceable lenses.&nbsp;Read our review.\n[Product: Kelty Low Loveseat | https://www.avantlink.com/click.php?tt=cl&merchant_id=b5770911-39dc-46ac-ba0f-b49dbb30c5c7&website_id=0f9b0f6f-13ac-4498-8e0f-b3beae765e07&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fb%2Fkelty-low-love-camp-chair%2F]\n* The&nbsp;Dyson Airwrap i.d.&nbsp;is available for $499.99 ($150 off) from Amazon,&nbsp;Best Buy&nbsp;and&nbsp;Dyson.&nbsp;The dryer can automatically adjust heat, airflow, and timing according to your styling preferences, with the app letting you set up a profile based on factors like your hair type, length, and skill level. From there, it can guide you through a more customized curling routine. Dyson also includes three attachments, including a conical barrel, a diffuser designed for waves and curls, and a blade concentrator.\n* The&nbsp;Amazfit Active 2&nbsp;is on sale for $89.99 ($10 off) at Amazon, which is $10 shy of its lowest price to date. It’s a surprisingly capable budget fitness tracker, with features like continuous heart rate and blood oxygen monitoring, offline navigation, and battery life that can last up to nine days. Read our review.\n[Product: BioLite Site Lights | https://www.amazon.com/BioLite-Lights-Lanterns-Camping-Outdoors/dp/B0DXQV785H/?tag=theverge02-20, https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bioliteenergy.com%2Fproducts%2Fsolar-site-lights%2F]\n[Product: BioLite FirePit Plus | https://go.skimresources.com/?id=1025X1701640&xs=1&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bioliteenergy.com%2Fproducts%2Ffirepit-plus, https://www.avantlink.com/click.php?tt=cl&merchant_id=b5770911-39dc-46ac-ba0f-b49dbb30c5c7&website_id=0f9b0f6f-13ac-4498-8e0f-b3beae765e07&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fbiolite-firepit]\nUpdate, May 26th: Updated to reflect current pricing / availability. Brandon Widder and Cameron Faulkner also contributed to this post.",
