    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-05-22-steve-wozniak-cheered-after-telling-students-they-have-ai-ac",
      "title": "Steve Wozniak cheered after telling students they have AI – actual intelligence",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.businessinsider.com/steve-wozniak-apple-ai-graduation-speech-2026-5\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48233563\nPoints: 519\n# Comments: 439",
      "body": "Steve Wozniak did what other college graduation commencement speakers couldn&apos;t this year: earn applause when talking about AI.The Apple cofounder took the stage during Grand Valley State University&apos;s graduation ceremony earlier this month. During his speech&comma; Wozniak offered reassurance to new graduates who are entering the workforce at the height of the AI revolution.&quot;You have AI — actual intelligence&comma;&quot; Wozniak said.The remark garnered laughs and applause from the audience.&quot;It would take too long to go deeply into what I think about AI&comma; but we&apos;ve been trying to create a brain&comma;&quot; Wozniak said. &quot;Is there a way we can duplicate a routine a trillion times and have it work like a brain? AI is one of those attempts.&quot;While Wozniak delivered his speech without interruption&comma; the same can&apos;t be said of some other AI-forward commencement speakers. In the weeks that followed&comma; former Google CEO Eric Schmidt and real estate executive Gloria Caulfield were both booed for their comments about AI at two separate graduate ceremonies.AI is looming over new graduates as they enter the job market. The tech is changing the landscape&comma; from the skills candidates need to how companies assess them. Its ability to automate many tasks has led some companies to conduct AI-related layoffs.During his commencement address&comma; Wozniak reflected on working at Apple and offered students some advice as they begin their careers.&quot;You should always try to think different&comma;&quot; he said. &quot;Don&apos;t follow the same steps as a million other people. Think&comma; is there something I can do a little different?&quot;",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Apple",
        "AI"
      ],
      "author": "signa11",
      "publishedAt": "2026-05-22T09:04:54.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://i.insider.com/6a0f3e9eb1025a62a5c85a84?width=1200&format=jpeg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.businessinsider.com/steve-wozniak-apple-ai-graduation-speech-2026-5",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-05-22-jessie-j-sobbed-for-hours-after-hearing-she-is-cancer-free",
      "title": "Jessie J 'sobbed for hours' after hearing she is cancer-free",
      "summary": "The singer says she \"exhaled for the first time in a year\" after doctors gave her the news.",
      "body": "3 hours agoHelen BushbyCulture reporterBBCThe singer, who announced she was diagnosed with breast cancer last year, said she went public to help process her diagnosis, and show solidarity with others going through a similar ordealSinger Jessie J has said she is now \"cancer free\", a year after revealing she had been diagnosed with breast cancer.In a video posted on Instagram on Thursday, the singer is seen waiting for an MRI scan as part of a yearly check-up. The caption reads: \"Results are in and I am cancer-free!\" followed by 10 crying emojis.She added: \"I sobbed for hours and then exhaled for the first time in a year.\"Jessie J said she decided to go public about her cancer in order to help process her diagnosis, and show solidarity with others going through a similar ordeal.The performer, who gave birth to a son in 2023, went on to say the diagnosis had given her \"incredible perspective\".\"But honestly I need to process it and talk about it and, I need a hug,\" she told fans.\"You have loved me through all my good and hard times. And I don't want this to be any different.\"The singer has had health issues throughout her life. She was diagnosed with a heart condition as a child, had a stroke as a teenager and briefly went deaf in 2020 due to Meniere's disease.'Nothing has broken me'In December last year, she told Women's Health: I've always had obscure health issues that [doctors] can't figure out. \"Nothing has broken me. And I believe I've gone through all the things I have to help people. Even if it's just to write songs about it.\"Jessie J has had three UK number one singles - Price Tag, Domino and Bang Bang (with Ariana Grande and Nicki Minaj). In 2011 the singer won the Brits critics' choice award, along with four Mobos - including best UK act and best album, for Who You Are.  She released her latest album, Don't Tease Me With A Good Time, in November 2025.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-05-22T09:02:50.000Z",
